<title>CHINA: China's Yantai to raise gold output to 35 tonnes.</title>
<headline>China's Yantai to raise gold output to 35 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's eastern coastal city of Yantai plans to boost gold output to 35 tonnes a year by the turn of the century, the China Daily Business Weekly said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The region in Shandong province produced 27.75 tonnes of gold last year, exceeding its target by 24.7 percent, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Proven gold reserves in Yantai represent one-third of China's total, it said.</p>
<p>In 1991-95, Yantai produced 113 tonnes of gold, earning pre-tax profits of 1.14 billion yuan ($137 million).</p>
